      "content": "If blistering begins, do not attempt to seal them with oil; this can trap infection underneath the skin. Blisters are your body's natural sterile dressing, and popping them introduces a high risk of infection. Instead of sealing, gently cover any blisters with sterile, non-adherent gauze to protect them from friction. If you notice the blisters getting larger, becoming cloudy, or if the surrounding area becomes hot and painful, please seek medical attention immediately.",
      "source": "target",
